# My everyday loaf based on morph

starter:
  ap_flour
  water
  hydration = 100%

leaven:
  starter
  bread_flour = 5 * starter
  cold_water
  extra = -20g
  hydration = 100%

wet:
  cold_water
  old_dough = 100g
  flourless_starter = 10%
  ascorbic_acid_1p = 50ppm * 100 * grain
  leaven = 40%
  olive_oil = 5%
  honey = 5%
  yogurt = 5%

grain:
  prairie_gold
  hard_red
  barley = 5%
  spelt = 5%
  buckwheat = 5%

dry:
  grain
  vwg = 3%
  potato_flakes = 5%
  yeast = 0.5%
  salt = 1.8%

dough:
  wet
  dry
  old_dough = 0 - wet.old_dough
  hydration = 70%
  # 200g/L of flour
  # total_flour = 660g # 13 inch
  total_flour = 500g # 9 inch
  # total = 1086g

/*
August 1, 2026

Changes
- Found my spelt!
- Use old dough and take it out at the end

Next time
- why was it 50g heavier than expected?
- was that why it was sticky?

Starter is 6 days old.

I started about 7:20

Mixed the leaven about 20:10 left on the counter. Initial T is 76.4.

Leaven pH = 3.67 at 7:58 dt is 75F. It rose to the top of the 500ml
container and had started to fall.

Dry T=89. Wet T=60. 

Used the KA for mixing. Mixed about 8:13. Stopped after 2 minutes;
it cleaned the bowl. DT after mixing is 72F. RT is 77F. 

30 minute rest in fridge.

Kneaded 7 minutes in KA. It was cleaning the bowl and looking great.

Into the cambro and the fridge at 8:20. S&F every 30 minutes.

Stickier than usual but managable. 

Into the pan at 10:14. Left on the counter at 77F.

100g of dough into fridge.

Baked at 11:45 for 45 minutes at 350F lid off.

I added 100ml of water to the pan before preheating the oven.

Beautiful loaf.
Super soft and delicious. More sour than the last.

*/

